# Project-init writers (idempotent — never overwrite user content).
_write_agents_md_stub() {
  cat > "${REPO_ROOT}/AGENTS.md" << 'AGENTS_EOF'
# AGENTS.md

Agent instructions for this project. Read by Claude Code, Codex, Cursor,
Aider, Gemini CLI, Copilot, and 60+ other tools — see https://agents.md/.

## Setup commands
<!-- e.g., `pnpm install`, `make setup` -->

## Build / test
<!-- e.g., `pnpm test`, `make test` -->

## Code style
<!-- e.g., TypeScript strict mode; single quotes; 2-space indent -->

## PR guidelines
<!-- e.g., one feature per PR; tests required; conventional commits -->

## yaamux runtime

This project uses yaamux (https://github.com/vihang/yaamux) to orchestrate
parallel agent worktrees. If you are reading this from inside a yaamux pane,
you have a set of environment variables that describe your situation:

| Var | What it tells you |
|-----|-------------------|
| `YAAMUX_AGENT_NAME`   | e.g. `agent-3` — your worktree directory name |
| `YAAMUX_AGENT_NUMBER` | 1-based, e.g. `3` |
| `YAAMUX_AGENT_TOTAL`  | total agents in this session |
| `YAAMUX_AGENT_TYPE`   | `claude` · `gemini` · `copilot` · `codex` |
| `YAAMUX_SESSION`      | tmux session name (e.g. `yaamux-myapp`) |
| `YAAMUX_PANE_ID`      | tmux pane id (e.g. `%23`) |
| `YAAMUX_REPO_ROOT`    | absolute path of the main checkout |
| `YAAMUX_VERSION`      | yaamux version string |
| `YAAMUX_AGENT_MODE`   | `safe` while you are an agent — destructive flags are refused |

Sibling agents live in worktrees `agent-1` … `agent-${YAAMUX_AGENT_TOTAL}`
next to the parent of `YAAMUX_REPO_ROOT`.

### Commands you can run from this shell

Read / inspect:
- `yaamux --list --json` — what other yaamux sessions are running on this machine
- `yaamux --status` — per-pane health of this session
- `yaamux --keys` — full CLI reference

Coordinate with siblings:
- `yaamux --send N "<prompt>"` — send a prompt to sibling agent N
- `yaamux --exec N "<cmd>" [timeout]` — synchronous: run + wait for completion

Background work (non-blocking):
- `yaamux --bg <name> "<cmd>"` — start a long-running command in a dedicated pane
- `yaamux --bg-tail <name> [--from N] [--follow]` — read its output from byte offset N
- `yaamux --bg-list [--json]` — see all background tasks with status
- `yaamux --bg-kill <name>` — stop a background task

Ship your work:
- `yaamux --pr <agent-number> "title"` — push + open a PR for the named agent's worktree

### Don't run these (human-owned)

These are refused while `YAAMUX_AGENT_MODE=safe` — leave to the operator:

- `yaamux --kill` — tears down the session you're running in
- `yaamux --clean` / `--clean --force` — removes worktrees (including yours)
- `yaamux --install` / `--uninstall` / `--install-service` — host-level config
AGENTS_EOF
}

